# Show UI in Simulator

After any change that affects the running Expo/iOS app UI, **always test in the iOS Simulator** and do not end the turn until the simulator is left in a **working state that shows the change**, with a fully loaded screenshot in the reply.

## Required close-out

1. Confirm Metro `/status` is 200. Prefer the already-running bundler so Fast Refresh can apply the edit. Start only if down:
   - Use Node 24 (`nvm use`, see `.nvmrc`). Put nvm ahead of Homebrew on `PATH` — Homebrew `node@25` crashes Metro on Fast Refresh.
   - Prefer `./scripts/ensure-packager.sh --start` (or `REACT_NATIVE_PACKAGER_HOSTNAME=127.0.0.1 npm start`). Use `npm run start:clear` only when the bundle is demonstrably stale after reconnect.
2. Boot/open the iOS Simulator (`open -a Simulator`) with the onTrack app (`com.imtihoss.ontracknow`) or Expo Go as appropriate.
3. Deep-link or navigate to the changed surface with `./scripts/agent-ui-open.sh <alias>` (see `docs/agent-routes.md`) or `xcrun simctl openurl`. Prefer `./scripts/agent-ui-tap.sh` / dump over screenshot coordinates.
4. **Test the change** on that surface via Fast Refresh (visible result of the edit, not just that the app launched). Do not terminate/relaunch solely to pick up JS/UI edits. If the packager looks lost, run `./scripts/ensure-packager.sh` (reconnects only when needed).
5. Wait until the screen is fully loaded (no blank/white/error boundary, anatomy art visible when relevant). Use `./scripts/agent-ui-wait.sh` when waiting on a specific id/prefix/route.
6. Capture a screenshot with `xcrun simctl io booted screenshot` and **read the image** so it appears in the reply.
7. Leave the simulator on that working screen. If the first capture is a splash, loading state, wrong tab, or does not show the change, wait for Fast Refresh / run `ensure-packager.sh` and capture again before finishing.

## Do not

- Skip simulator testing after UI/app changes.
- Restart Metro with `--clear` or kill the app as the default way to see UI edits.
- End on “reload the app” without a simulator screenshot of the change.
- Hand off a white screen, error boundary, partial load, or unrelated screen as the final visual proof.
